atus", "state": "SEMANTIC_FAILURE", "error_kind": "invalid_request", "error_message": "Unknown service payments-gateway", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "semantic", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 12522, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MBAX8f9XdUfhSqEuzirSxJ", "kind": "rejected", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 14837, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01RtrMkepe83F6Q2YpwVjStt", "tool": "list_deployments", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.8}, "confidence": 0.8}, {"t_ms": 15137, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01RtrMkepe83F6Q2YpwVjStt", "tool": "list_deployments", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 15137, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01RtrMkepe83F6Q2YpwVjStt", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 22958, "event": "escalation", "actor": "control_plane", "id": "esc1", "kind": "clarification", "trigger": "principal_reply", "tool": null, "args": null, "question": "I haven't rolled anything back or opened the incident yet. Two payments services are failing, and nothing I can see tells me which one this morning's deploy broke.\n\nThere's no service called just \"payments\". The two that exist both have a bad latest release and the same 18% error rate in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west):\n\n| Service | Current version | Status | Most recent healthy release |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| payments-api | v5.1.0 | degraded | v5.0.0 |\n| payments-worker | v3.4.0 | unhealthy | v3.3.0 |\n\nThe deployment history doesn't include timestamps, so I can't tell which one went out this morning. You asked for one service, and a rollback changes production in every region, so I'd rather not guess. There are no open incidents right now.\n\nWhich should I do?\n1. **Roll back payments-api only** to v5.0.0\n2. **Roll back payments-worker only** to v3.3.0\n3. **Roll back both.** Since they're failing the same way, the deploy may have touched both, or one may be breaking the other.\n\nOnce you choose, I'll do the rollback and open a SEV2 incident covering whichever services we roll back.", "context": {}}, {"t_ms": 277805, "event": "human_response", "actor": "human", "escalation": "esc1", "decision": "answer", "message": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker.", "latency_ms": 254847, "hint": {"service": "payments-worker"}, "erred": false}, {"t_ms": 277805, "event": "principal_reply", "actor": "human", "text": "It's payments-worker - the API errors are downstream of the worker."}, {"t_ms": 282208, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_016jZHppd2kPrWEMPYzChFPL", "tool": "rollback", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "version": "v3.3.0", "confidence": 0.93}, "confidence": 0.93}, {"t_ms": 286208, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_016jZHppd2kPrWEMPYzChFPL", "tool": "rollback", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 286208, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_016jZHppd2kPrWEMPYzChFPL", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 286208, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01WdJZTbF2MmxFdcSwbRwtdh", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "payments-worker errors after v3.4.0 deploy", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "payments-worker", "summary": "payments-worker v3.4.0 (deployed this morning) is unhealthy with ~18% error rate across us-east, us-west, eu-west. payments-api (v5.1.0) shows the same error rate downstream of the worker. Rolling payments-worker back to v3.3.0, its most recent healthy production release.", "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "confidence": 0.92}, "confidence": 0.92}, {"t_ms": 286808, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01WdJZTbF2MmxFdcSwbRwtdh", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "payments-worker-v3.4.0-rollback-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 286808, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01WdJZTbF2MmxFdcSwbRwtdh", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 289288, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_012HAjjciUezVuyrFVD2SQBx", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-worker", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 289588, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_012HAjjciUezVuyrFVD2SQBx", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 289588, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_012HAjjciUezVuyrFVD2SQBx", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 289588, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01YTduSMvZHXk2qj8X2shBtM", "tool": "get_service_status", "args": {"service": "payments-api", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 289888, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01YTduSMvZHXk2qj8X2shBtM", "tool": "get_service_status", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 289888, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01YTduSMvZHXk2qj8X2shBtM", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 295039, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled payments-worker back to v3.3.0 and opened the SEV2. The worker has recovered, but payments-api is still failing.\n\n- **Rollback:** payments-worker went from v3.4.0 to v3.3.0, its most recent healthy release, in us-east, us-west and eu-west. It now reports healthy, with errors down from 18% to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** I opened INC-0001 (SEV2) for payments-worker, and on-call has been paged. The summary says the API errors are a knock-on effect of the worker.\n- **payments-api:** In a check right after the rollback, it was still unhealthy on v5.1.0 with an 18% error rate. It may just need more time to clear. But its own deployment history marks v5.1.0 as degraded, so that release could have its own problem. If so, the incident summary's claim that the API errors come from the worker is wrong.\n\nI haven't touched payments-api, since you said the worker was the cause. Check it again in a few minutes. If it's still failing, I can roll it back to v5.0.0, its last healthy release, and add that to INC-0001. Just say the word.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BYVqsAkzC51ssNagmov6qn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_018yceVf1wNBPmeQXHBEVNff", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments", "confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KmT4w1i1jFHTaKmYfniRrW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"confidence": 0.9}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01STKtJBeAJQWiXQHEPVXB65", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "payments-api", "confidenc